{title: 257 - Come Down, O Love Divine}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #257 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 257}
{meta: category Holy Spirit - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D/F#]Come down, [A]O Love [D]divine, [A/E]seek thou this [G]soul of [Em]mine
[F#m]and visit [A]it with thine [G/D]own ardor [A/E]glowing;
[D/F#]O Comforter, [A]draw near, [F#m]within [A/E]my heart [G]appear,
[Em/G]and kindle [D/A]it, [Em/B]thy [Bm]holy flame [A]bestowing.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D/F#]O let [A]it freely [D]burn, [A/E]till earthly [G]passions [Em]turn
[F#m]to dust and [A]ashes in [G/D]its heat consuming;
[D/F#]and let [A]thy glorious light [F#m]shine [G]ever [A/E]on [G]my [D/A]sight,
[Em/G]and clothe [D/A]me round, [Em/B]the while [Bm]my path [A]illuming.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D/F#]Let holy [A]charity Mine outward [G]vesture [Em]be,
[F#m]And lowliness [A]become [G/D]my inner [A/E]clothing;
[D/F#]True lowliness [A]of heart [F#m]which takes [A/E]the humbler [D/A]part,
[Em/G]And o'er [D/A]its own [Em/B]shortcomings [Bm]weeps [A]with loathing.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D/F#]And so [A]the yearning [D]strong [A/E]with which the [G]soul will [Em]long
[F#m]shall far outpass [A]the power [G/D]of human [A/E]telling;
[D/F#]for none [A]can guess its [F#m]grace, till [G]Love [A/E]create [G]a [D/A]place
[Em/G]wherein [D/A]the Holy [Em/B]Spirit [Bm]makes [A]a dwelling.
{end_of_verse}
